<title>SINGAPORE: IPC Corp sells unit to AMC.</title>
<headline>IPC Corp sells unit to AMC.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Personal computer maker IPC Corp Ltd said on Friday it had sold its IPCA unit to Asia Media Communications Ltd (AMC) for Australia $1.00.</p>
<p>IPC said in a statement that under the deal, IPCA would assign debts of U.S. $25 million it owes to AMC International Holdings (AIH) to AIH, which would issue US$25 million of its redeemable preference stock to IPC.</p>
<p>The stock can be exchanged for shares in AMC at US$2.00 per share, the statement said.  </p>
<p>IPC said the deal was in the best interests of the group as IPCA had not made a positive contribution to results. It said the sale should not have any material adverse impact on earnings.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
